<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/images/favicon.png" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/images/icon.png" />
    <title>About · Daily Story</title>

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/index.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/about.css">

</head>
<body>
    <div class="grain" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <!-- ============ HEADER ============ -->
    <header class="site-header">
        <a class="brand" href="/">
            <span class="brand-dot"></span>
            <span class="brand-name">Daily Story</span>
        </a>
        <nav class="site-nav">
            <a href="/" class="nav-strong">Read today's story</a>
            <% if (typeof isLoggedIn !== 'undefined' && isLoggedIn) { %>
                <form action="/logout" method="post" class="nav-form">
                    <button type="submit">Sign out</button>
                </form>
            <% } else { %>
                <a href="/login">Log in</a>
                <a href="/signup">Sign up</a>
            <% } %>
        </nav>
    </header>

    <!-- ============ ARTICLE ============ -->
    <main class="column about-main">
        <div class="title-block">
            <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
            <h1>A short story a day, at exactly your level.</h1>
            <p class="about-lead">
                Daily Story gives you one fresh conversation to read every
                morning — written by AI in the language you're learning,
                with three quick questions to check you followed along.
            </p>
        </div>

        <section class="about-section">
            <h2>How it works</h2>
            <ol class="steps">
                <li>
                    <strong>Choose your language.</strong>
                    English, Spanish, French, German, Italian, Portuguese,
                    Chinese, or Japanese.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Pick your level.</strong>
                    Four levels from beginner to advanced, so the story meets
                    you where you are.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Read and check yourself.</strong>
                    Read today's conversation, then answer three comprehension
                    questions.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Come back tomorrow.</strong>
                    Bookmark your page — a new story lands every morning.
                </li>
            </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="about-section">
            <h2>Find your level</h2>
            <p>
                Levels follow the CEFR, the common standard for measuring
                language ability. Here's what each one feels like:
            </p>

            <div class="about-levels">
                <div class="about-level">
                    <span class="about-level-cefr">A1</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Beginner</h3>
                        <p>Simple conversations with everyday phrases and basic vocabulary — ordering food, asking directions, greeting friends.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="about-level">
                    <span class="about-level-cefr">A2</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Conversational</h3>
                        <p>Short exchanges about familiar topics — making plans, talking about hobbies, sharing simple opinions.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="about-level">
                    <span class="about-level-cefr">B1</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Intermediate</h3>
                        <p>Everyday and moderately complex discussions — experiences, viewpoints, professional emails, comparing options.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="about-level">
                    <span class="about-level-cefr">B2</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Advanced</h3>
                        <p>In-depth discussion of concrete and abstract topics — debates, analysis, and nuanced language.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="about-section">
            <h2>Tips for best results</h2>
            <ul class="tips">
                <li>Start one level below where you think you are — building confidence beats struggling.</li>
                <li>Don't worry about every word. Focus on getting the main idea.</li>
                <li>Use the quiz to check comprehension, not just vocabulary.</li>
                <li>Read daily. Even five minutes counts.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="about-section">
            <h2>Open source</h2>
            <p>
                Daily Story is open source. Check out the code, contribute, or
                report issues on
                <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/appdevjohn/daily-story" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
            </p>
        </section>

        <div class="about-cta">
            <a href="/" class="btn-cta">Read today's story →</a>
        </div>
    </main>

    <%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
